 context_blocks=[block('The textbook proves a characteristic-time lower bound and discusses matching it asymptotically as the error probability vanishes at a fixed instance. Its broader research discussion does not equate that limit with a uniform finite-time theorem.'),block('The 2014 paper states the two-arm iterated-logarithm lower bound, deriving it from Farrell’s 1964 sequential-testing result. A positive limsup as the unknown gap tends to zero contradicts the selected uniform bound.','resolution'),block('A September 2026 preprint claims a broader gap-entropy characterization. Its stated uniform upper bound explicitly retains an additive iterated-logarithm term. The present archival rests on the established two-arm obstruction, not on verification of that new preprint’s full proofs.','recent')],
